<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Taifa of Guadix</h1><p class="st-meta">1145 CE – 1151 CE (approx.) · capital Guadix</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived highland taifa around Guadix and Baza, east of Granada, formed during the revolts against the Almoravids.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1145, as the Almoravid regime in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> disintegrated, local leaders took control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadix">Guadix</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baza">Baza</a>, two towns on the high plateau between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> and the coast at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almeria">Almería</a> region.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Known only from brief chronicle references, the state was centred on irrigated basins and cave settlements and controlled the route from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> to the east coast. Its leaders were caught between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-mardanish">Ibn Mardanish</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murcia">Murcia</a>, the Almoravid loyalists of Granada and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 1151 the district passed under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> control. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadix">Guadix</a> later belonged to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/emirate-of-granada">Emirate of Granada</a> until 1489.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1145 CE – 1151 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:82.49%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1145 CE – 1151 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Guadix</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Andalusi Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Taifa of Guadix and Baza</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1148&amp;focus=taifa-of-guadix" aria-label="Taifa of Guadix on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4602 835 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Taifa of Guadix lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4922 1091L4799 1289M4922 1091L4794 1282"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4799 1289h0M4794 1282h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4922 1091h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4922 1091h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Guadix. <a href="/atlas?year=1148&amp;focus=taifa-of-guadix">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
